<%# The one control, on both pages an account is signed in or created on: the same
    callback answers either, so the label names the action rather than the page.

    The request phase answers POST alone and the middleware answers it with a
    redirect to Google, so this form must not be Turbo's: a fetch cannot follow the
    visitor to Google and back. The authenticity token button_to adds is what
    omniauth-rails_csrf_protection checks before the middleware runs. %>
<div class="google-sign-in">
  <%= button_to t("accounts.google.continue"),
        "/auth/google_oauth2",
        method: :post,
        class: "button button-secondary button-google",
        form: { data: { turbo: false } } %>
</div>
